  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reintroduction of Black Rhinos to Sera Wildlife Conservancy, Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will assist with the costs of establishing the first eastern black rhino reintroduction site on community-owned land in Kenya. The site has been fenced to include a closed rhino sanctuary of 120 km2, and has been approved to receive rhinos from the national authority, Kenya Wildlife Services, in 2014. Specific activities will include 1) completion of the electric fencing, gates, and ranger bases and accommodation, 2) equipping rangers with vehicles and communications equipment and 3) conducting ground and air patrols, 4) construct temporary holding pens for rhinos on site, 5) translocate rhinos from elsewhere in Kenya, install tracking equipment, and 6) release and track the animals and conduct post-release monitoring and veterinary interventions, as necessary.</narrative>
  </description>
